WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.280 --> 00:00:03.749
Hi, and welcome to Fabric!

2
00:00:03.749 --> 00:00:04.960
In the next two minutes,

3
00:00:04.960 --> 00:00:09.200
I'll show you how Fabric turns everyday conversations about your work…

4
00:00:09.200 --> 00:00:11.770
into clear, living process maps.

5
00:00:12.577 --> 00:00:14.337
This is your workspace.

6
00:00:14.337 --> 00:00:16.657
On the left is the Process Tree:

7
00:00:16.657 --> 00:00:19.627
your organization, laid out as functions,

8
00:00:19.697 --> 00:00:22.377
departments, and the processes inside them.

9
00:00:22.377 --> 00:00:24.537
Click to expand any branch…

10
00:00:24.537 --> 00:00:28.507
or press Control K to jump straight to a process by name.

11
00:00:29.075 --> 00:00:31.601
Every process has its own page,

12
00:00:31.601 --> 00:00:33.915
and this is where it all starts.

13
00:00:33.915 --> 00:00:35.635
Hit Start AI interview,

14
00:00:35.635 --> 00:00:39.715
and Fabric's voice agent will talk you through how the work really gets done:

15
00:00:39.715 --> 00:00:41.275
the steps, the tools,

16
00:00:41.275 --> 00:00:42.492
the handoffs.

17
00:00:42.492 --> 00:00:43.875
Prefer to go solo?

18
00:00:43.875 --> 00:00:44.875
Record a voice note,

19
00:00:44.875 --> 00:00:47.325
or upload a recording you already have.

20
00:00:47.871 --> 00:00:50.831
Every interview lands in the Conversations tab,

21
00:00:50.831 --> 00:00:53.031
with the audio, an AI summary,

22
00:00:53.031 --> 00:00:56.121
and a full transcript you can read and replay.

23
00:00:56.768 --> 00:00:59.458
Now here's where it gets interesting.

24
00:00:59.488 --> 00:01:04.795
Fabric reads across every conversation and writes a single overview of the process.

25
00:01:04.795 --> 00:01:06.581
It shows where people agree,

26
00:01:06.581 --> 00:01:08.328
where their accounts differ…

27
00:01:08.328 --> 00:01:10.768
and which sources back up each point.

28
00:01:10.768 --> 00:01:12.368
The more people you interview,

29
00:01:12.368 --> 00:01:14.218
the sharper the picture gets.

30
00:01:14.779 --> 00:01:18.139
Open Process Flow to see it all as a map:

31
00:01:18.139 --> 00:01:20.899
every step, decision, and handoff,

32
00:01:20.899 --> 00:01:23.259
built from what people actually said.

33
00:01:23.259 --> 00:01:25.499
Bottlenecks are flagged right on the steps,

34
00:01:25.499 --> 00:01:27.989
so you can spot the friction at a glance.

35
00:01:28.560 --> 00:01:31.600
Insights rolls it all up into the numbers:

36
00:01:31.600 --> 00:01:34.560
steps, handoffs, tools, decisions,

37
00:01:34.560 --> 00:01:38.650
and pain points, each one traced back to the evidence.

38
00:01:39.412 --> 00:01:41.846
And finally, Automations.

39
00:01:41.846 --> 00:01:46.966
Fabric recommends where workflows and AI agents could take work off people's plates…

40
00:01:46.966 --> 00:01:50.656
and writes a ready-to-paste brief for Copilot Studio.

41
00:01:51.448 --> 00:01:52.888
So that's Fabric.

42
00:01:52.888 --> 00:01:54.688
Pick a process you know well,

43
00:01:54.688 --> 00:01:56.448
hit Start AI interview,

44
00:01:56.448 --> 00:01:57.677
and just talk.

45
00:01:57.677 --> 00:01:59.298
We'll take care of the rest!
